DC Motor Control Simulation

I used Mokxi to simulate DC motor control with an ESP32-S3, a transistor, resistor, and a 3.7 V battery. My goal was to understand PWM control before working with the 8520 motors for my SKYGUARD drone.

I successfully controlled my motor speed using three levels: 100/255, 200/255, and 255/255 (details in the code).

I encountered unexpected motor speeds and very low voltage readings. My next step is to check the wiring and understand the simulation results (details in the circuit).
